<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Add Your Organization — {{.SiteName}}</title>
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Montserrat:wght@400;600;700;800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="css/styles.css">
    <script src="js/nav.js" defer></script>
</head>
<body>

    {{template "nav" .}}

    <main class="mission-page">
        <h1>Add Your Organization</h1>

        <p>{{.SiteName}} is an open-source project and welcomes contributions from advocacy organizations working in this space. Adding your organization takes just a few minutes using the GitHub website — no coding experience or local setup required.</p>

        <h2>What you will need</h2>
        <p>A free <a href="https://github.com" target="_blank">GitHub account</a>. That's it.</p>

        <h2>Step-by-step</h2>

        <p><strong>1. Open the organizations file on GitHub</strong><br>
        Go to <a href="https://github.com/hollingv/iwebsite/blob/main/src/cmd/gacli/organizations.go" target="_blank"><code>src/cmd/gacli/organizations.go</code></a> in the repository and click the <em>pencil icon</em> (Edit this file) in the top right of the file view.</p>

        <p><strong>2. Add your organization</strong><br>
        Find the <code>OrgGroup</code> that best fits your work (Legal, Medical, or Informational) and add a new entry following this pattern:</p>

        <pre><code>{{.ContributeExample}}</code></pre>

        <p><strong>3. Propose your change</strong><br>
        Scroll down to the <em>Commit changes</em> section. Write a brief commit message such as <code>feat: add Your Organization Name</code>. Select <em>Create a new branch and start a pull request</em>, then click <em>Propose changes</em>.</p>

        <p><strong>4. Submit the pull request</strong><br>
        GitHub will take you to a pull request form. Add a short description of your organization and click <em>Create pull request</em>. A maintainer will review and merge your submission — GitHub handles the forking automatically behind the scenes.</p>

        <h2>URL conventions</h2>
        <p>To be automatically included in the knowledge base and future aggregation features, we encourage organizations to publish content at consistent paths:</p>

        <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Path</th><th>Content</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>/about</code></td><td>About your organization</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>/research</code></td><td>Research and evidence</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>/news</code></td><td>News and press coverage</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>/events</code></td><td>Upcoming events</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>/legal-cases</code></td><td>Active or completed legal cases</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <p>Organizations that follow these conventions are integrated into the hub automatically with no manual effort required.</p>

        <div class="tagline">Learn. Understand. Take action.</div>
    </main>

    {{template "footer" .}}

</body>
</html>
